319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 645 0 R
/T (Class and Concept: Bavdegalutamide is a PROTAC \(PROteolysis TArgeting Chimera\), a heterobifunctional molecule designed to degrade the androgen receptor \(AR\) protein rather than just blocking its function.)
/E (Class and Concept: Bavdegalutamide is a PROTAC \(PROteolysis TArgeting Chimera\), a heterobifunctional molecule designed to degrade the androgen receptor \(AR\) protein rather than just blocking its function.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 646 0 R
/E (Binding to Androgen Receptor \(AR\): Bavdegalutamide specifically binds to the ligand-binding domain \(LBD\) of the androgen receptor on prostate cancer cells. This binding is achieved through a chemical moiety \(cyclohexyl or aryloxy cyclohexane\) that fits into the AR's ligand pocket, similar to how natural hormones or antagonists bind.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 647 0 R
/E (Recruitment of E3 Ubiquitin Ligase Complex: Bavdegalutamide has a second functional domain that binds an E3 ubiquitin ligase complex, specifically one containing cereblon \(CRBN\). Cereblon is an E3 ligase that facilitates the tagging of proteins with ubiquitin molecules.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 648 0 R
/E (Ubiquitination: Once the PROTAC molecule brings AR and the cereblon E3 ligase into close proximity, the E3 ligase catalyzes the transfer of ubiquitin chains onto the AR protein. This polyubiquitination marks the AR for degradation.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 649 0 R
/E (Proteasomal Degradation: The polyubiquitinated AR is recognized by the 26S proteasome \(a cellular complex responsible for protein degradation\), which unfolds and degrades the AR protein into small peptides, effectively removing it from the cell.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 650 0 R
/E (Outcome: By degrading the AR protein itself, rather than merely inhibiting its ligand binding, Bavdegalutamide shuts down downstream androgen signaling pathways that drive prostate cancer cell growth and survival. This is particularly effective against cancers with mutations or amplifications in AR that confer resistance to traditional AR antagonists.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 651 0 R
/T <>
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 652 0 R
/T (Pharmacologic Action: The PROTAC effect is catalytic; one molecule of Bavdegalutamide can induce degradation of multiple AR proteins by repeatedly recruiting cereblon and the proteasome.)
/E (Pharmacologic Action: The PROTAC effect is catalytic; one molecule of Bavdegalutamide can induce degradation of multiple AR proteins by repeatedly recruiting cereblon and the proteasome.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
